From 41206ea212b4bbbbab12866cbcdaeeb31c4c0e0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 14:46:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(wardrobe): add Wardrobe Analysis page behind the grid
 chip row
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a third "Analysis" chip alongside the filter and sort chips on the
wardrobe grid, opening a new WardrobeAnalysis screen with derived stats:
headline counters, a category-balance donut, a style profile with an
expandable insight, a colour distribution strip, and most/least worn rows.

There is no backend analysis endpoint, so every figure is derived on the
client from data the app already fetches — the wardrobe list (read from the
grid's own query cache, so arriving from the grid paints instantly), the
favourites total and the creations list. The four derivation modules are
pure and unit-tested:

- category: one bucket per item via the backend's category synonyms, with
  precedence so overlapping families can't double-count
- style: independent shares (an item can be both minimal and casual), with
  the app's own control tags (fit:*, favorite, less-used) excluded
- colour: normalises color_hex / dominant_color / colors into 13 named
  buckets, testing chroma before hue so near-neutrals stay neutral
- worn: delegates ordering to sortWardrobeItems so these rows and the
  grid's "Most worn" sort can't disagree

Also moves FAVOURITES_QUERY_KEY into favouriteService so the analysis
counter and the Favourite page share one cache entry instead of each
issuing its own GET /favorites.

Chart and swatch palettes go in theme.ds.color; the token lint now skips
__tests__, where a hex is a fixture rather than a styling decision.
