+### 5.4.b Wardrobe Analysis (derived-stats page)
+
+Reached from the "Analysis" chip in the wardrobe grid's filter/sort row. Every
+figure on the page is derived client-side from the wardrobe / favourites /
+creations the app already holds — there is no analysis endpoint, so there are no
+server-side events to correlate against.
+
+| Event | Trigger | Location | Properties |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `wardrobe_analysis_opened` | "Analysis" chip tapped in the wardrobe chip row | `WardrobeScreen.tsx` (`handleOpenAnalysis`) | `item_count` (wardrobe size at open), `category` (filter active on the grid — `All` or the joined selection) |
+| `wardrobe_analysis_viewed` | Analysis screen focused with its item query settled — fires on focus, so a back-navigation re-fires it | `WardrobeAnalysisScreen.tsx` | `item_count` |
+| `wardrobe_analysis_insight_toggled` | Style-insight card tapped (expands/collapses the longer explanation in place) | `WardrobeAnalysisScreen.tsx` (`handleToggleInsight`) | `expanded` (bool — state AFTER the tap), `style?` (`minimal`/`casual`/`classic`/`soft`/`bold` — omitted when no item carries a style signal) |
+| `wardrobe_analysis_item_opened` | Tile tapped in the most-worn or least-worn row → ItemDetail | `WardrobeAnalysisScreen.tsx` (`handleOpenItem`) | `item_id`, `source` (`most_worn` / `least_worn`) |
+
+No PII: no colour hex, no item names, no free-text. `style` is a fixed
+five-value enum, `source` a two-value enum.
+
 ### 5.5 Favourite + try-on outcomes
 
